WEBVTT

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.740
That yellow one...

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.910
Um... This one?

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.910
Yeah... please.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.420
Is this for you?

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.590
Are you in love with Rokka?

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.220
How long have you been here?

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.010
Three years.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.180
She's my wife.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.350
I'm Shimao Atsushi.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.850
Um, I mean, Shimao, what are you?

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.270
I'm surprised, too, since you can see me...

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.950
He was a strange guy.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.280
He'd tell me to get a divorce when he died...

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.080
And to throw away all of his belongings...

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.000
Not even understanding how I felt...

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.460
Your husband's wishes are important, aren't they?

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.460
So...

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.260
I mean...

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.720
For example... you could...

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.010
have an affair with me or something...

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:21.280
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:27.450
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:34.000
I was prepared for the time you left

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:40.840
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:47.350
After I embraced you with all I had

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:56.900
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:00.570
filled my heart

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:07.070
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:13.750
You gave me happiness

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:17.080
Until I meet you again one day

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.580
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.130
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:26.800
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.930
I won't forget your smile

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.440
<i>My right ear was slightly hard of hearing,</i>

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:45.200
<i>stemming from a high fever I had as a child.</i>

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:51.620
<i>So she would usually walk on my left side.</i>

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.750
<i>That was my unspoken reserved spot.</i>

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.550
<i>Oh!</i>

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.470
<i>Has it already been a week since Hazuki and I had ramen for lunch together?</i>

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.100
<i>I can't even tell if it's been a long time or not.</i>

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.190
You're in love with me?

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.600
Yes, I am!

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.110
<i>That's what he said,</i>

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.480
<i>but nothing's happened after that.</i>

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.110
<i>What was that?</i>

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.120
Manager.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:36.120
Yes?

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:42.630
This lady is asking whether Chilean evening primrose and fourwing evening primrose are the same.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.800
They're different kinds.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.630
Really?

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:50.390
Those flowers have similar names and looks, so people often mix them up.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.260
Which one are you looking for?

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.260
Evening primrose.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.770
In that case, you're looking for these.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:59.650
Then please make a small bouquet with these as the main flower.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.770
With the Chilean evening primrose?

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:02.270
Yes.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.280
Certainly.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.240
<i>But in the language of flowers...</i>

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:13.030
<i>it means fickleness or capriciousness.</i>

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:14.870
<i>Should I say something?</i>

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:20.790
<i>Maybe Hazuki is a Chilean evening primrose, too.</i>

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.290
I'm gonna carry this to the back.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:33.220
<i>In the end, I spent the manager's birthday taking turns minding the shop with Miho.</i>

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:40.140
<i>With my shallow thinking, I couldn't come up with any kind of birthday present that would make the manager happy,</i>

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:46.150
<i>so after the store closed, I used the wages I made that day to buy a huge pot of Kookaburra and brought it home.</i>

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:50.320
<i>I couldn't think of anything except helping the store out as a customer.</i>

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:55.450
<i>I'd do anything to make the manager happy if I could only figure out what would.</i>

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.040
Hey, Hazuki...

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.040
You're really a chicken, huh?

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.670
Nah. It's not my fault somebody got in my way.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:06.300
Who did?

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.590
You've been a real pain in the ass lately.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.640
That shit's really annoying.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:16.010
What's with the thing you do every time I talk to the manager?

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.600
Make faces?

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.270
It's childish.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.650
You said such noble things to her face,

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.980
but in reality, you're just an annoying, clingy husband.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.020
You're going too far!

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.070
I don't think so.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:28.780
I'm normal!

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:29.690
My ass.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:32.240
You're acting like a complete louse.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:37.990
Every time I approach the manager, I get the perfect view of the back of your head.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.500
Anybody would lose the will to fight.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.750
You're the one who made your wife cry, so I don't think you have any right to interfere.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:46.880
You're right.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:50.210
But life just doesn't work out the way we want it to.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.220
That sounds depressing coming from me, right?

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.340
There's some truth to it, though.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.390
Now that I'm here, it gets me thinking...

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.890
Which of us goes through more pain?

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:04.150
The one who's gone or the one who's left behind?

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:10.780
<i>I thought I cried a lifetime's worth of tears.</i>

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.160
<i>It was pitch-black ahead</i>

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:18.330
<i>and I was so confused that I didn't even know where to put my hands.</i>

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:24.170
<i>He didn't come back to life during the wake, and now he's nothing but bones.</i>

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.420
<i>What saved me up until now was keeping myself busy.</i>

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:31.590
<i>Makes me wonder, "why me?"</i>

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.760
<i>I think Hazuki is much younger than me...</i>

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.770
<i>The girls should be all over him.</i>

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:47.770
Um...

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:48.940
Yes.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.150
Manager...

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.150
Yes?

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.450
<i>He doesn't know when to quit...</i>

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:57.910
What is it?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:05.410
U-Um, after we close the shop tonight, would you like to go out for dinner somewhere?

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:07.710
Dinner?

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:08.540
Yeah.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.090
<i>He can't even look at me.</i>

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:11.550
<i>Maybe he's shy...</i>

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.840
<i>If I can get the manager out of here, I win!</i>

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:16.630
Sure.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.180
Thank you.

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:24.980
Where do you want to eat?

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:27.230
What I said before...

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.730
Have you given it any thought?

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.150
I did.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:36.990
I've thought about quite a bit.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:38.360
Really?

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:40.990
Have you really thought about it, Hazuki?

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:41.990
Well, of course...

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:43.830
I mean, I've already gone through one husband.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.870
I wonder if there's really any merit in choosing me.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.090
Would going by merits make it easier to decide?

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:52.130
Sure it would.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.420
It would?

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.380
Uh-huh.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:57.550
In that case, dating me has many merits.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:58.510
"In that case?"

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.180
Am I right?

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.800
I don't know...

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:01.720
Never mind.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:02.830
So it doesn't matter.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:08.270
<i>My place was always at her right side.</i>

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:11.150
<i>But now...</i>

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:14.320
<i>What a life.</i>

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:18.700
<i>Hey,</i>

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:20.360
<i>Rokka.</i>

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:24.290
<i>I was always happy.</i>

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.660
<i>I got to be with the woman I love...</i>

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:32.590
No...

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:34.630
No...

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.010
No, don't go...

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.720
Please, stay with me...

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.390
Don't leave me alone!

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:55.650
<i>When my time came, it was just the two of us...</i>

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.910
<i>You told me not to leave,</i>

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:02.820
<i>so I...</i>

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.620
<i>decided I wouldn't go anywhere.</i>

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.080
Delicious!

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.630
The cheese is great!

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.340
I wonder what this one is...

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:18.800
Garlic!

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.760
<i>Why, of all things...</i>

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.350
<i>My breath probably stinks.</i>

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:29.600
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:33.150
<i>it feels like my right shoulder is being tickled a little.</i>

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:39.860
<i>It's been so long since I've sat next to a man like this.</i>

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:41.570
Was it spicy?

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:43.700
Not particularly...

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:44.780
Maybe it was the chili oil...

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:45.870
I'm fine.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.540
The food here is really good, isn't it?

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:52.750
It's famous, right?

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:53.420
Yeah.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.750
It was featured in a magazine.

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.380
Although I knew about it before that.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.560
<i>This brings back memories.</i>

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.600
<i>If I keep going along like this, in a daze,</i>

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.360
<i>will I eventually sleep with Hazuki?</i>

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:19.360
<i>Maybe I'll just take what I can get.</i>

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:25.200
<i>Until last week, I never would've imagined having an affair.</i>

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.540
<i>It's embarrassing.</i>

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.870
<i>I'm actually a little excited.</i>

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:51.270
We must smell awful, huh?

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:54.520
See you tomorrow.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.400
W-W-Wait a second!

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.270
If you follow me now, we're through!

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:17.790
Drink some water...

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.380
Yes?

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:28.890
Special delivery.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:32.260
Yes?

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:32.970
You have a package.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.430
Thank you.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:44.150
Um... Your seal...

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:45.650
Right.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.410
Is it okay if I just sign for it?

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.280
Sure, that's fine.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:54.040
I told you we'd be through...

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.630
I didn't think you'd actually carry out that threat.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:03.800
You have a point.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.630
Sorry for acting so silly.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:11.140
When you put it that way, you make me feel like I'm on top of the world.

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:15.020
The thing is, I intended to do it anyway.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:20.140
And because you let me in so easily, you got my hopes up.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:23.270
This is what I wanted to do all along...

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:24.900
So...

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.150
Manager.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:29.910
I'm not gonna be turned off just because you smell like garlic.

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:34.240
Hazuki...

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.500
<i>She closed her eyes!</i>

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:46.000
<i>So annoying... Get out of the way, ghost!</i>

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:49.470
<i>Give it up already.</i>

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:50.930
<i>This is ridiculous.</i>

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:53.680
I won't let anyone have her.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:57.310
Your true colors are finally showing.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:01.560
I'm gonna make her forget all about her pathetic husband.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:03.310
Huh?

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.070
U-Um...

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.290
<i>Shit...</i>

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.290
<i>That was meant for </i>him<i>.</i>

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:29.420
Manager...

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.010
I apologize.

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:35.390
Now that's...

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:36.220
What?

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.810
Whatever, just go.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.020
Don't scowl like that.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:01.540
What?

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:02.790
Um...

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.250
Uh... I love you!

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:10.510
Ow! Ow! Ow! Why?!

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:12.510
Don't say it so nonchalantly.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.340
Go home...

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.280
<i>Going back and forth like a pendulum, at my age...</i>

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:33.990
Manager.

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:36.450
Good night.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:41.830
<i>I'm ashamed of myself...</i>

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:57.640
<i>For the first time in my life, I almost want to kill someone.</i>

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:02.020
<i>And unfortunately, he's already dead.</i>

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:05.560
I want to make Rokka happy.

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.230
I won't let anyone have her.

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.730
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:14.740
<b>22 years old
Resume
Hazuki
Ryousuke</b>

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:17.860
<i>He's eight years younger than me?!</i>

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:21.030
<i>He does do cute things.</i>

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.450
<i>I was on the verge of getting swept away.</i>

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.460
<i>Close call...</i>

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:34.970
<i>I think it's been a long time...</i>

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:39.260
<i>since you last sighed, Rokka.</i>

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:46.060
<i>After I was hospitalized, you never let me see you exhausted.</i>

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.190
The shop is fine.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:52.520
Miho and the others will help out until you're ready to go back to work, Shimao.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:54.480
The doctor was here earlier.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:58.950
He said we won't be able to have kids.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.870
For one, I had radiation therapy long ago.

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:03.740
Yeah.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:06.620
That's not why I'm doing this, though.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:07.660
<b>Divorce Registration Papers</b>

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:07.710
Here. I had my sister get it for me.
<b>Divorce Registration Papers</b>

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:11.130
<b>Divorce Registration Papers
Here. I had my sister get it for me.</b>

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.880
I've already put my seal on my part.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:19.430
With my current condition, I don't think we need to worry.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.390
I think this is the first time I've seen one of these.

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:22.640
Hey!

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:30.650
You know,

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:34.780
I love your flower arrangements more than anyone else's in the whole world.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:40.990
Even now, I remember the day I first saw your work at vocational school.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:46.660
I thought, "So this is what it means to arrange flowers like they're still flowers."

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:52.420
Unlike the ones that were overly-arranged and fake or the ones that stood out because of their unconventionality,

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:59.010
the look you were going for affirmed the beauty of the flowers, even if they were dropping petals or dying.

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:02.640
For better or for worse,

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.310
for richer or poorer,

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.850
in sickness and in health...

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:10.890
Never underestimate your wife.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.560
As long as you're alive, we're golden.

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:22.240
I will haunt you...

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:27.540
You can't sleep like this.

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:30.960
You'll catch a cold.

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:33.540
Come on...

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.000
Hey...

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.420
Rokka.

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.180
Uh-oh...

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.020
My joints are killing me.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.650
Ow...

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.900
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:00.110
That's why I kept saying to sleep under the blankets!

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:04.610
<i>I'm this close to her, yet I can't even cover her with a blanket.</i>

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.910
Time to go to the auction already?

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:12.040
Should probably ask someone to cover the shop first.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:15.130
Can I even drive like this?

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.000
No, you can't!

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.710
You just took medicine for your fever, right?

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:21.170
Oh, boy.

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.720
Now I feel dizzy...

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:24.380
See?

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:30.220
But if I don't take a shower...

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:32.390
Idiot! Are you trying to make it worse?!

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:36.690
Guess... I'll send a text...

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:37.860
Hey!

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:39.360
Hey!

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:41.190
Rokka!

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:47.660
Damn it...

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:52.000
Thought I heard that ghost's voice just now.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:55.830
And he was yelling the manager's name...

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:56.960
That's a bad omen.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.920
An empty text?

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:03.380
Why?

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:08.680
Hello?

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.810
Hazuki, good morning.

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.140
Miho...

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:14.850
Did you get a text from Rokka?

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:16.900
Yeah. Um...

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:18.900
I got a text but something was wrong.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:21.150
Mine was blank.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:22.690
I wonder if something happened...

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:23.690
Dunno.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.830
Trying to be the hero?

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:37.710
Really?

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:41.020
Fuck, I don't wanna deal with a belligerent ghost first thing in the morning.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:42.050
Never mind, just hurry up!

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.800
Go around the back. The keys are under the bronze princess flowerpot, second in the back row!

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.340
What princess?

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:48.890
The brown succulent!

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:52.140
<i>I'm the only one who can see her husband,</i>

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:56.180
<i>so if anyone sees me following his instructions, they'll think I'm a trespasser.</i>

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:58.770
That one...

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:10.490
Anyone home?

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:17.290
Manager!

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:20.040
You're burning up!

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:21.840
Sorry...

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:26.090
Sorry... Shimao...

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.430
The bedroom is over there.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:30.590
The doorway you can see.

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:35.100
There's medicine in the basket next to the phone.

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:38.100
If she's out of cooling gel strips, there's an ice pack in the freezer.

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.270
She had a vitamin drink just a bit ago.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:48.400
Shimao...

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:52.320
Please don't worry about the shop.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:56.950
Miho is going to open the shop on time and we'll use what we have in stock.

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:01.210
Shimao...

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:07.130
I'm...

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.050
so sorry...

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:19.810
<i>I'm the one who wants to cry.</i>

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:26.440
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:32.200
you always smile

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:36.280
Tell me why

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:40.160
it won't go away

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.960
I gave you everything

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:43.790
You gave me everything

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:48.590
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:48.590 --> 00:21:50.260
still my everything

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:53.470
I love you

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:56.850
The songs of midsummer days

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:59.970
are a fleeting miracle

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:05.940
like the winter snow

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:12.950
If I hadn't met you

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:16.160
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:23.670
and nothing would have pressed down on my dreams

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:29.340
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:36.390
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:41.520
When I close my eyes

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:45.520
you're right beside me
